{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_bd058aca8e5dfc8cef20fa6f06bb6874e49aff4f97554781c4845725c7cc5e39", "title": "Lee Roy Selmon's", "text": "Lee Roy Selmon's is an American casual dining restaurant chain located and founded in Florida by former NFL player Lee Roy Selmon. The concept was owned by OSI Restaurant Partners, LLC until 2008 when it was sold to Mvp Holdings Tampa, Inc. owned by Outback Steakhouse founders Robert D. \"Bob\" Basham and Chris T. Sullivan. Lee Roy Selmon continued to work with the company through its transfer of ownership until his death in 2011. There are eight locations, all of which are located in west-central Florida.", "score": 8.7519}, {"id": "hp_doc_5e4b542e3de84a25a53b238b81af5b680a5f574c1fe414ac35af6f762b0eddc5", "title": "Roy Chapman", "text": "Roy Clifford Chapman (18 March 1934 – 21 March 1983) was an English professional footballer and manager, born in Birmingham. He was the father of former Arsenal and Leeds United striker Lee Chapman.", "score": 8.5726}, {"id": "hp_doc_c02f0d699b5e07c6fe171bf330c556ad53309e4866404731e0ba6b0688d070d0", "title": "Lawrence Bittaker and Roy Norris", "text": "Lawrence Sigmund Bittaker (born September 27, 1940) and Roy Lewis Norris (born February 5, 1948) are American serial killers and rapists known as the Tool Box Killers, who together committed the kidnap, rape, torture, and murder of five teenage girls over a period of five months in southern California in 1979.", "score": 7.8361}], "remaining_searches": 2}
